#   Comments + Keyword Clarification

#    Anton, Calculus, 0.4.24
# DESCRIPTION
# Given area constraint, determine the measurements of a box that generates the greatest volume.

# ENDDESCRIPTION
## DBsubject(Calculus - single variable)
## DBchapter(Applications of differentiation)
## DBsection(Optimization - general)
## Institution(John Wiley & Sons)
## MLT(BoxOpenTopMaxVol)
## Level(5)
## MO(1)
## TitleText1('Calculus')
## AuthorText1('Anton')
## EditionText1('9')
## Section1('4.5')
## Problem1('24')
## KEYWORDS('Functions', 'Applied Problems', 'Maximize', 'Area', 'Volume', 'Optimization')
DOCUMENT();
loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'contextFraction.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');


#    The box is made from $A sq ft of material. It has a square base (side S) and vertical sides (H)
#       Area = $A = S^2 + 4SH (open top)
#       Volume = (S^2)H

#       H = ($A - S^2)/4S, so V(S) = ($AS - S^3)/4

#       V'(S) = ($A - 3S^2)/4  ==> = 0 at S = sqrt(A/3) 
Context("Numeric")->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0, reduceConstantFunctions=>0);

$A = random(200,3000,100);

#   Base length in lowest terms
$n = $A;
$d = 3;

$com = gcd($A,3);

($n, $d) = ($n/$com, $d/$com);
# ($n,$d,$wnum) = reduce_fraction($n,$d);
if ($wnum > 0)
{
  $Base = Formula("sqrt($wnum)");
  ($wnum,$nnum,$snum,$simp) = sqrt_simplify($wnum);
  if ($nnum != 1) 
  {
    $Extra1 = "= $simp";
    if ($snum == 1)
    {
      $tmp = Formula("$nnum/2")->reduce;
      $Extra2 = "= $tmp";
    }
    else
    {
      $tmp = Formula("$nnum/2")->reduce;
      $Extra2 = "= $tmp \sqrt{$snum}";
    }
  }
  else
  {
    ($Extra1,$Extra2) = "";
  }
}
else
{
  $Base = Formula("sqrt($n/$d)");
  ($Extra1,$Extra2) = "";
}
$Height = Formula("(1/2) $Base");
Context()->variables->add(S=>'Real',H=>'Real');
$Hform = Formula("($A - S^2)/(4 S)")->reduce;
$Hformeval = Formula("($A - $Base^2)/(4 $Base)");
$Areaform = Formula("S^2 + 4*S*H")->reduce;
$Vofs = Formula("($A S - S^3)/4");
$Vprime = Formula("($A - 3 S^2)/4");

BEGIN_PGML
A container with square base, vertical sides, and open top is to be made from [$A] ft[`^2`] of material.
Find the dimensions of the container with greatest volume. If appropriate, leave your answer in radical form
and enter all fractions in lowest terms.

a) Length of Base: [_]{$Base}

b) Height: [_]{$Height}
END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
If we refer to the length of a side of the base as [`S`] and the height as [`H`], then
the volume of the box is,
[```V = S^2H```]
Since the box has an open top, the surface area is comprised of the base ([`S^2`]) and the 4 sides
([`4SH`]). Therefore, the surface area of the box is,
[```A = S^2 + 4SH = [$A]```]
Solving for [`H`] we get [``H = [$Hform]``], and we substitute this into the formula
for volume to get,
[```V = S^2\left([$Hform]\right) \quad \Rightarrow V(S) = [$Vofs]```]
To find the maximum volume, differentiate and set equal to 0:
[```V\;'(S) = [$Vprime] \quad \Rightarrow V\;'(S) = 0\; \mbox{when} \;S = [$Base] [$Extra1]```]
To find the corresponding value for the height,
[```h = [$Hformeval] = [$Height] [$Extra2]```]

END_PGML_SOLUTION
ENDDOCUMENT();